rule = ("Task 1, the rule as cycles/006/theme-currency-lists.work/census2.py applies it (cycle 18 and 19 census.py scripts are a different test: they replay sync and settle in callTracer frames, they do not balance flows). "
 "Inputs per block range: ERC-20 Transfer logs with the PoolManager as topic1 (out) or topic2 (in), counted only when the log has exactly three topics and 32 bytes of data (census2.py:69); WETH style Deposit(dst) logs naming the PoolManager, counted as in (census2.py:73-74); "
 "and every PoolManager log: Swap amounts as signed int128, Donate amounts, ModifyLiquidity pool ids, Initialize keys, and ERC-6909 Transfer logs with from = 0 (claims minted) or to = 0 (claims burned) (census2.py:76-91). "
 "Per transaction and currency: net = out + minted - in - burned; owed = sum of Swap amount0/amount1 of pools holding the currency, positive when the pool pays, minus Donate amounts (census2.py:106-111). "
 "A row is flagged only when net > owed and the transaction holds no ModifyLiquidity log of a pool with that currency (skipped-liquidity) and no pool event on a pool missing from the Initialize list (skipped-unknown-pool) (census2.py:118-123). "
 "Hook deltas have no event (src/PoolManager.sol:181, 224) and enter only through the Transfer and claim logs they cause; protocol fee collection has no event (src/ProtocolFees.sol:44-57) and is recognised afterwards by rule.py from the trace (collectProtocolFees output) or from a fall of protocolFeesAccrued (cycles/006/theme-currency-lists.work/rule.py:171, 185). "
 "Native currency: a native transfer leaves no log, so a native row exists only when a claim of id 0 is minted or burned, or on Arc where 0xff..fe Transfer logs exist; on every other network such rows are counted as native-no-logs and skipped (census2.py:116). "
 "What the rule cannot see: (a) every native outflow on 20 of 21 networks; (b) any currency of a pool that has a ModifyLiquidity log in the same transaction, because the event carries liquidityDelta and no amounts (src/PoolManager.sol:175), so an outflow dressed as a liquidity removal or fee collection is never judged; (c) pools absent from the Initialize list; "
 "(d) a wrong amount that the PoolManager itself computes and logs: the Swap event is emitted from the same delta that is paid (src/PoolManager.sol:234-251), so an arithmetic fault in Pool.swap, SwapMath, SqrtPriceMath or FullMath that overpays a swapper is booked as owed and never flagged; this census therefore cannot test the opcode and integer library hypotheses of this cycle, which the mined swap replays in OPCODES.md test instead; "
 "(e) ERC-6909 transfers between accounts (from and to both nonzero, src/ERC6909.sol:30, 45), so claims moved from a victim and then burned for a take net to zero; (f) balance changes without a standard Transfer log, in either direction (rebases, mints that log only Deposit, tokens with nonstandard events); (g) freezes, which move nothing; (h) the flag is one sided: an inflow larger than owed is not reported.")
cleared.append(dict(chainIds=ALL, lens='L6', check=rule[:rule.index('. Inputs') + 1], result=rule, source='research/network-risk/cycles/006/theme-currency-lists.work/census2.py:1-125; research/network-risk/cycles/006/theme-currency-lists.work/rule.py:1-190; src/PoolManager.sol:175; src/PoolManager.sol:241'))
